2. Begin standing, and raise vos bras out to the side holding the implements. vos bras should be parallel to the ground. In competition, judges or sensors are used to let you know when you break parallel. Hold for as long as you can. Typically, the poids should be heavy enough that you fail in 30-60 seconds.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Crucifix/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Crunch - Hands Overhead', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Allongez-vous au sol with votre dos flat and genous bent with around a angle de 60 degrés between the ischio-jambiers and the mollets.
2. Keep vos pieds flat on le sol and stretch vos bras overhead with your palms crossed. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Curl your upper body forward and bring your omoplates just off le sol. en permanence, keep vos bras aligned with votre tête, neck and épaule. Don''t move them forward from that position. Expirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement and hold the contraction for a second.
4. Lentement, lower down to the position de départ as you inspirez.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Crunch_-_Hands_Overhead/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Crunch - Legs On Exercise Ball', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Allongez-vous au sol with vos pieds resting on an exercise ball and your genous bent at a angle de 90 degrés.
2. Place vos pieds three to four inches apart and point your toes inward so they touch.
3. Place vos mains lightly on either side of votre tête keeping your coudes in. Conseil : Don''t lock your fingers behind votre tête.
4. Push the small of votre dos down in le sol in order to better isolate your abdominal muscles. C''est votre position de départ.
5. Begin to roll your épaules off le sol and continue to push down as hard as you can with your lower back. Your épaules should come up off le sol only about four inches, and your lower back should remain on le sol. Expirez as you execute this portion of le mouvement. Squeeze your abdominals hard at the top of the contraction and Maintenez la position 1 seconde. Conseil : Focus on a slow, controlled movement. Refrain from using momentum at any time.
6. Lentement, go back down to the position de départ as you inspirez.
7. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Crunch_-_Legs_On_Exercise_Ball/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Crunches', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Allongez-vous au sol with vos pieds flat on the ground, or resting on a banc with your genous bent at a angle de 90 degrés. If you are resting vos pieds on a banc, place them three to four inches apart and point your toes inward so they touch.
2. Now place vos mains lightly on either side of votre tête keeping your coudes in. Conseil : Don''t lock your fingers behind votre tête.
3. While pushing the small of votre dos down in le sol to better isolate your abdominal muscles, begin to roll your épaules off le sol.
4. Continue to push down as hard as you can with your lower back as you contract your abdominals and expirez. Your épaules should come up off le sol only about four inches, and your lower back should remain on le sol. At the top of le mouvement, contract your abdominals hard and keep the contraction for a second. Conseil : Focus on slow, controlled movement - don''t cheat yourself by using momentum.
5. After the one second contraction, begin to come down Lentement, again to the position de départ as you inspirez.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Crunches/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Cuban Press', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Take a haltère in each hand with a pronated grip in a standing position. Raise your upper arms so that they are parallèle au sol, allowing your lower arms to hang in the "scarecrow" position. C''est votre position de départ.
2. To initiate le mouvement, externally rotate the épaules to move the upper arm 180 degrees. Keep the upper arms in place, rotating the upper arms until the poignets are directly above the coudes, the forearms perpendiculaire à le sol.
3. Now press the haltères by extending at the coudes, straightening vos bras overhead.
4. Revenez en position de départ as you Inspirez by reversing the steps.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Cuban_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dancer''s Stretch', 'Bas du dos', 'Autre', '1. Sit up on le sol.
2. Cross your right leg over your left, keeping the genou bent. Your left leg is straight and down on le sol.
3. Place your left arm on your right leg and your right hand on le sol.
4. Rotate your upper body to the right, and Maintenez 10-20 secondes. Switch sides.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abducteurs, Fessiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dancers_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dead Bug', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Begin lying on votre dos with vos mains extended above you toward the ceiling.
2. Bring vos pieds, genous, and hanches up to 90 degrees.
3. Expirez hard to bring your ribcage down and flatten votre dos onto le sol, rotating your pelvis up and squeezing your fessiers. Hold this position throughout le mouvement. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Initiate the exercise by extending one leg, straightening the genou and hanche to bring the leg just above the ground.
5. Maintain the position of your lumbar and pelvis as you perform le mouvement, as votre dos is going to want to arch.
6. Stay tight and return the working leg to the position de départ.
7. Répétez de l''autre côté, alternating until the set is complete.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dead_Bug/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Deadlift with Bands', 'Bas du dos', 'Barre', '1. To deadlift with short bands, simply loop them over the bar before you start, and step into them to set up. For long bands, they will need to be anchored to a secure base, such as heavy haltères or a rack.
2. With vos pieds, and your grip set, take a big breath and then lower your hanches and bend the genous until your shins contact the bar. Look forward with votre tête, keep your poitrine up and votre dos arched, and begin driving through the heels to move the poids upward. After the bar passes the genous, aggressively pull the bar back, pulling your omoplates together as you drive your hanches forward into the bar.
3. Lower the bar by bending at the hanches and guiding it to le sol.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Milieu du dos, Quadriceps, Trapèzes. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Deadlift_with_Bands/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Deadlift with Chains', 'Bas du dos', 'Barre', '1. You can attach the chains to the sleeves of the bar, or just drape the middle over the bar so there is a greater poids increase as you lift.
2. Approach the bar so that it is centered over vos pieds. You feet should be about hanche width apart. Bend at the hanche to grip the bar at épaule width, allowing your omoplates to protract. Typically, you would use an prise en pronation or an over/under grip on heavier sets. With vos pieds, and your grip set, take a big breath and then lower your hanches and bend the genous until your shins contact the bar.
3. Look forward with votre tête, keep your poitrine up and votre dos arched, and begin driving through the heels to move the poids upward. After the bar passes the genous, aggressively pull the bar back, pulling your omoplates together as you drive your hanches forward into the bar.
4. Lower the bar by bending at the hanches and guiding it to le sol.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Milieu du dos, Quadriceps, Trapèzes. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Deadlift_with_Chains/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Decline Barbell Bench Press', 'Pectoraux', 'Barre', '1. Secure vos jambes at the end of the decline banc and Lentement, lay down on the banc.
2. Using a prise moyenne (a grip that creates a angle de 90 degrés in the middle of le mouvement between the forearms and the upper arms), lift the bar from the rack and hold it straight over you with vos bras locked. The arms should be perpendiculaire à le sol. C''est votre position de départ. Conseil : In order to protect your rotator cuff, it is best if you have a spotter help you lift the barre off the rack.
3. As you Inspirez, come down Lentement, until you feel the bar on your lower poitrine.
4. Après une pause, bring the bar back to the position de départ as you Expirez and push the bar using your poitrine muscles. Lock vos bras and squeeze your poitrine in the contracted position, Maintenez la position 1 seconde and then start coming down Lentement, again. Conseil : It should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up).
5. Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.
6. When you are done, place the bar back in the rack.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Decline_Barbell_Bench_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Decline Close-Grip Bench To Skull Crusher', 'Triceps', 'Barre', '1. Secure vos jambes at the end of the decline banc and Lentement, lay down on the banc.
2. Using a close grip (a grip that is slightly less than épaule width), lift the bar from the rack and hold it straight over you with vos bras locked and coudes in. The arms should be perpendiculaire à le sol. C''est votre position de départ. Conseil : In order to protect your rotator cuff, it is best if you have a spotter help you lift the barre off the rack.
3. Now lower the bar down to your lower poitrine as you Inspirez. Keep the coudes in as you perform this movement.
4. Using the triceps to push the bar back up, press it back to the position de départ as you expirez.
5. As you Inspirez and you keep the upper arms stationary, bring the bar down Lentement, by moving your forearms in a semicircular motion towards you until you feel the bar slightly touch your forehead. Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement.
6. Lift the bar back to the position de départ by contracting the triceps and exhaling.
7. Répétez steps 3-6 until the recommended amount of repetitions is performed.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Decline_Close-Grip_Bench_To_Skull_Crusher/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Decline Crunch', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Secure vos jambes at the end of the decline banc and lie down.
2. Now place vos mains lightly on either side of votre tête keeping your coudes in. Conseil : Don''t lock your fingers behind votre tête.
3. While pushing the small of votre dos down in the banc to better isolate your abdominal muscles, begin to roll your épaules off it.
4. Continue to push down as hard as you can with your lower back as you contract your abdominals and expirez. Your épaules should come up off the banc only about four inches, and your lower back should remain on the banc. At the top of le mouvement, contract your abdominals hard and keep the contraction for a second. Conseil : Focus on slow, controlled movement - don''t cheat yourself by using momentum.
5. After the one second contraction, begin to come down Lentement, again to the position de départ as you inspirez.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Decline_Crunch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Decline Dumbbell Bench Press', 'Pectoraux', 'Haltères', '1. Secure vos jambes at the end of the decline banc and lie down with a haltère on each hand on top of your cuisses. The palms of your hand will be facing each other.
2. Once you are laying down, move the haltères in front of you at épaule width.
3. Once at épaule width, rotate your poignets forward so that the palms of vos mains are facing away from you. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Bring down the poids Lentement, to your side as you Expirez. Keep full control of the haltères en permanence. Conseil : Throughout the motion, the forearms should always be perpendiculaire à le sol.
5. As you Expirez, push the haltères up using your pectoral muscles. Lock vos bras in the contracted position, squeeze your poitrine, Maintenez la position 1 seconde and then start coming down slowly. Conseil : It should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up..
6. Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions of your training program.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Decline_Dumbbell_Bench_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Decline Dumbbell Flyes', 'Pectoraux', 'Haltères', '1. Secure vos jambes at the end of the decline banc and lie down with a haltère on each hand on top of your cuisses. The palms of your hand will be facing each other.
2. Once you are laying down, move the haltères in front of you at épaule width. The palms of the hands should be facing each other and the arms should be perpendiculaire à le sol and fully extended. C''est votre position de départ.
3. With a slight bend on your coudes in order to prevent stress at the biceps tendon, lower vos bras out at both sides in a wide arc until you feel a stretch on your poitrine. Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : Keep in mind that throughout le mouvement, the arms should remain stationary; le mouvement should only occur at the épaule joint.
4. Return vos bras back to the position de départ as you squeeze your poitrine muscles and Expirez. Conseil : Make sure to use the same arc of motion used to lower the poids.
5. Maintenez la position 1 seconde at the contracted position and Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Decline_Dumbbell_Flyes/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Decline Dumbbell Triceps Extension', 'Triceps', 'Haltères', '1. Secure vos jambes at the end of the decline banc and lie down with a haltère on each hand on top of your cuisses. The palms of your hand will be facing each other.
2. Once you are laying down, move the haltères in front of you at épaule width. The palms of the hands should be facing each other and the arms should be perpendiculaire à le sol and fully extended. C''est votre position de départ.
3. As you Inspirez and you keep the upper arms stationary (and coudes in), bring the haltères down Lentement, by moving your forearms in a semicircular motion towards you until your thumbs are next to your ears. Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement.
4. Lift the haltères back to the position de départ by contracting the triceps and exhaling.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Decline_Dumbbell_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Decline EZ Bar Triceps Extension', 'Triceps', 'Barre', '1. Secure vos jambes at the end of the decline banc and Lentement, lay down on the banc.
2. Using a close grip (a grip that is slightly less than épaule width), lift the EZ bar from the rack and hold it straight over you with vos bras locked and coudes in. The arms should be perpendiculaire à le sol. C''est votre position de départ. Conseil : In order to protect your rotator cuff, it is best if you have a spotter help you lift the barre off the rack.
3. As you Inspirez and you keep the upper arms stationary, bring the bar down Lentement, by moving your forearms in a semicircular motion towards you until you feel the bar slightly touch your forehead. Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement.
4. Lift the bar back to the position de départ by contracting the triceps and exhaling.
5. Répétez until the recommended amount of repetitions is performed.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Decline_EZ_Bar_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Decline Oblique Crunch', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Secure vos jambes at the end of the decline banc and Lentement, lay down on the banc.
2. Raise your upper body off the banc until your torse is about 35-45 degrees if measured from le sol.
3. Put one hand beside votre tête and the other on your cuisse. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Raise your upper body Lentement, from the position de départ while turning your torse to the left. Continue crunching up as you expirez until your right coude touches your left genou. Hold this contracted position for a second. Conseil : Focus on keeping your abdominaux tight and keeping le mouvement slow and controlled.
5. Lower votre corps back down Lentement, to the position de départ as you inspirez.
6. After completing one set on the right for the recommended amount of repetitions, switch to your left side. Conseil : Focus on really twisting your torse and feeling the contraction when you are in the up position.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Decline_Oblique_Crunch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Decline Push-Up', 'Pectoraux', 'Autre', '1. Allongez-vous au sol face down and place vos mains about 36 inches apart while holding your torse up bras tendus. Move vos pieds up to a box or banc. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Next, lower yourself downward until your poitrine almost touches le sol as you inspirez.
3. Now Expirez and press your upper body back up to the position de départ while squeezing your poitrine.
4. Après une pause, at the top contracted position, you can begin to lower yourself downward again for as many repetitions as needed.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Decline_Push-Up/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Decline Reverse Crunch', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Allongez-vous au sol on a decline banc and hold on to the top of the banc with both hands. Don''t let votre corps slip down from this position.
2. Hold vos jambes parallèle au sol using your abdominaux to hold them there while keeping your genous and feet together. Conseil : vos jambes should be fully extended with a slight bend on the genou. C''est votre position de départ.
3. While exhaling, move vos jambes towards the torse as you roll your pelvis backwards and you raise your hanches off the banc. At the end of this movement your genous will be touching your poitrine.
4. Hold the contraction for a second and move vos jambes back to the position de départ while inhaling.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Decline_Reverse_Crunch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Decline Smith Press', 'Pectoraux', 'Machine', '1. Place a decline banc underneath the Smith machine. Now place the barre at a height that you can reach when lying down and vos bras are almost fully extended. Using a pronated grip that is wider than épaule width, unlock the bar from the rack and hold it straight over you with vos bras extended. C''est votre position de départ.
2. As you inspirez, lower the bar under control by allowing the coudes to flex, lightly contacting the torse.
3. Après une pause, bring the bar back to the position de départ by extending the coudes, exhaling as you do so.
4. Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.
5. When the set is complete, lock the bar back in the rack.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Decline_Smith_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Deficit Deadlift', 'Bas du dos', 'Barre', '1. Begin by having a platform or poids plates that you can stand on, usually 1-3 inches in height. Approach the bar so that it is centered over vos pieds. You feet should be about hanche width apart. Bend at the hanche to grip the bar at épaule width, allowing your omoplates to protract. Typically, you would use an prise en pronation or an over/under grip on heavier sets.
2. With vos pieds, and your grip set, take a big breath and then lower your hanches and bend the genous until your shins contact the bar. Look forward with votre tête, keep your poitrine up and votre dos arched, and begin driving through the heels to move the poids upward. After the bar passes the genous, aggressively pull the bar back, pulling your omoplates together as you drive your hanches forward into the bar.
3. Lower the bar by bending at the hanches and guiding it to le sol.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Milieu du dos, Quadriceps, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Deficit_Deadlift/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Depth Jump Leap', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. For this drill you will need two boxes or benches, one 12 to 16 inches high and the other 22 to 26 inches high.
2. Stand on one of the two boxes with arms at the sides; feet should be together and slightly off the edge as in the depth jump. Place the other box approximately two or three feet in front of and facing the performer.
3. Begin by dropping off the initial box, landing and simultaneously taking off with both feet.
4. Rebound by driving upward and outward as intensely as possible, using the arms and full extension of the body to jump onto the higher box. Again, allow the legs to absorb the impact.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abducteurs, Adducteurs, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Depth_Jump_Leap/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dip Machine', 'Triceps', 'Machine', '1. Sit securely in a dip machine, select the poids and firmly grasp the handles.
2. Now keep your coudes in at your sides in order to place emphasis on the triceps. The coudes should be bent at a angle de 90 degrés.
3. As you contract the triceps, extend vos bras downwards as you expirez. Conseil : At the bottom of le mouvement, focus on keeping a little bend in vos bras to keep tension on the triceps muscle.
4. Now Lentement, let vos bras come back up to the position de départ as you inspirez.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dip_Machine/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dips - Chest Version', 'Pectoraux', 'Autre', '1. For cet exercice you will need access to parallel bars. To get yourself into the position de départ, hold votre corps bras tendus (arms locked) above the bars.
2. While breathing in, lower yourself Lentement, with your torse leaning forward around 30 degrees or so and your coudes flared out slightly until you feel a slight stretch in the poitrine.
3. Once you feel the stretch, use your poitrine to bring votre corps back to the position de départ as you Expirez. Conseil : Remember to squeeze the poitrine at the top of le mouvement for a second.
4. Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dips_-_Chest_Version/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dips - Triceps Version', 'Triceps', 'Poids de corps', '1. To get into the position de départ, hold votre corps at arm''s length with vos bras nearly locked above the bars.
2. Now, inspirez and Lentement, lower yourself downward. Your torse should remain upright and your coudes should stay close to votre corps. This helps to better focus on triceps involvement. Lower yourself until there is a angle de 90 degrés formed between the upper arm and forearm.
3. Then, expirez and push your torse back up using your triceps to bring votre corps back to the position de départ.
4. Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dips_-_Triceps_Version/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Donkey Calf Raises', 'Mollets', 'Autre', '1. For cet exercice you will need access to a donkey calf raise machine. Start by positioning your lower back and hanches under the padded lever provided. The tailbone area should be the one making contact with the pad.
2. Place both of vos bras on the side handles and place the balls of vos pieds on the calf block with the heels extending off. Align the toes forward, inward or outward, depending on the area you wish to target, and straighten the genous without locking them. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Raise your heels as you Expirez by extending your chevilles as high as possible and flexing your calf. Ensure that the genou is kept stationary en permanence. There should be no bending at any time. Hold the contracted position by a second before you start to go back down.
4. Go back Lentement, to the position de départ as you Inspirez by lowering your heels as you bend the chevilles until mollets are stretched.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Donkey_Calf_Raises/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Double Kettlebell Alternating Hang Clean', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Kettlebell', '1. Place two kettlebells between vos pieds. To get in the position de départ, push your butt back and look straight ahead.
2. Clean one kettlebell to your épaule and hold on to the other kettlebell.
3. With a fluid motion, lower the top kettlebell while driving the bottom kettlebell up.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Mollets, Avant-bras, Fessiers, Bas du dos, Quadriceps, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Double_Kettlebell_Alternating_Hang_Clean/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Double Kettlebell Jerk', 'Épaules', 'Kettlebell', '1. Hold a kettlebell by the handle in each hand.
2. Clean the kettlebells to your épaules by extending through the legs and hanches as you pull the kettlebells towards your épaules. Rotate your poignets as you do so, so that the palms face forward. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Dip votre corps by bending the genous, keeping your torse upright.
4. Immediately reverse direction, driving through the heels, in essence jumping to create momentum.
5. As you do so, press the kettlebells overhead to lockout by extending the arms, using votre corps''s momentum to move the poids.
6. Return vos pieds to the ground in a split fashion, with one foot forward and one foot back.
7. Keeping the poids overhead, return to a standing position, bringing vos pieds together. Lower the poids to perform the next repetition.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Quadriceps, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Double_Kettlebell_Jerk/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Double Kettlebell Push Press', 'Épaules', 'Kettlebell', '1. Clean two kettlebells to your épaules.
2. Squat down a few inches and reverse the motion rapidly. Use the momentum from the legs to drive the kettlebells overhead.
3. Once the kettlebells are locked out, lower the kettlebells to your épaules and Répétez.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Quadriceps, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Double_Kettlebell_Push_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Double Kettlebell Snatch', 'Épaules', 'Kettlebell', '1. Place two kettlebells behind vos pieds. Bend your genous and sit back to pick up the kettlebells.
2. Swing the kettlebells between vos jambes forcefully and reverse the direction.
3. Drive through with your hanches and lock the ketttlebells overhead in one uninterrupted motion.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Quadriceps. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Double_Kettlebell_Snatch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Double Kettlebell Windmill', 'Abdominaux', 'Kettlebell', '1. Place a kettlebell in front of your front foot and clean and press a kettlebell overhead with your opposite arm. Clean the kettlebell to your épaule by extending through the legs and hanches as you pull the kettlebell towards your épaules. Rotate your poignet as you do so, so that the palm faces forward.
2. Keeping the kettlebell locked out en permanence, push your butt out in the direction of the locked out kettlebell. Turn vos pieds out at a forty-five degree angle from the arm with the locked out kettlebell.
3. Bending at the hanche to one side, sticking your butt out, Lentement, lean until you can retrieve the kettlebell from le sol. Keep your eyes on the kettlebell that you hold over votre tête en permanence.
4. Pause for a second after retrieving the kettlebell from the ground and reverse the motion back to the position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Double_Kettlebell_Windmill/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Double Leg Butt Kick', 'Quadriceps', 'Poids de corps', '1. Begin standing with your genous slightly bent.
2. Quickly squat a short distance, flexing the hanches and genous, and immediately extend to jump for maximum vertical height.
3. As you go up, tuck your heels by flexing the genous, attempting to touch the buttocks.
4. Finish the motion by landing with the genous only partially bent, using vos jambes to absorb the impact.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abducteurs, Adducteurs, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Double_Leg_Butt_Kick/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Downward Facing Balance', 'Fessiers', 'Swiss ball', '1. Lie facedown on top of an exercise ball.
2. While resting on your stomach on the ball, walk vos mains forward along le sol and lift vos jambes, extending your coudes and genous.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Downward_Facing_Balance/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Drag Curl', 'Biceps', 'Barre', '1. Grab a barre with a supinated grip (paumes vers l''avant) and get your coudes close to your torse and back. C''est votre position de départ.
2. As you expirez, curl the bar up while keeping the coudes to the back as you "Drag" the bar up by keeping it in contact with your torse. Conseil : As you can see, you will not be keeping the coudes pinned to your sides, but instead you will be bringing them back. Also, do not lift your épaules.
3. Lentement, go back to the position de départ as you keep the bar in contact with the torse en permanence.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Drag_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Drop Push', 'Pectoraux', 'Autre', '1. Position low boxes or other platforms 2-3 feet apart.
2. Move to a pushup position between them, supporting yourself by placing vos mains on the boxes.
3. With good posture, drop from the platforms by pressing up and moving vos mains to épaule width, cushioning your landing by absorbing the impact through the arm.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Drop_Push/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dumbbell Alternate Bicep Curl', 'Biceps', 'Haltères', '1. Stand (torse upright) with a haltère in each hand held bras tendus. The coudes should be close to the torse and the palms of your hand should be facing your cuisses.
2. While holding the upper arm stationary, curl the right poids as you rotate the palm of the hands until they are facing forward. At this point continue contracting the biceps as you Expirez until your biceps is entièrement contracté and the haltères are at épaule level. Maintenez la position 1 seconde as you squeeze the biceps. Conseil : Only the forearms should move.
3. Lentement, begin to bring the haltère back to the position de départ as your Inspirez. Conseil : Remember to twist the palms back to the position de départ (facing your cuisses) as you come down.
4. Répétez le mouvement with the left hand. This equals one repetition.
5. Continue alternating in this manner for the recommended amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Alternate_Bicep_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dumbbell Bench Press', 'Pectoraux', 'Haltères', '1. Allongez-vous sur un banc plat with a haltère in each hand resting on top of your cuisses. The palms of vos mains will be facing each other.
2. Then, using your cuisses to help raise the haltères up, lift the haltères one at a time so that you can hold them in front of you at épaule width.
3. Once at épaule width, rotate your poignets forward so that the palms of vos mains are facing away from you. The haltères should be just to the sides of your poitrine, with your upper arm and forearm creating a angle de 90 degrés. Be sure to maintain full control of the haltères en permanence. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Then, as you Expirez, use your poitrine to push the haltères up. Lock vos bras at the top of the lift and squeeze your poitrine, Maintenez la position 1 seconde and then begin coming down slowly. Conseil : Ideally, lowering the poids should take about twice as long as raising it.
5. Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions of your training program.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Bench_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dumbbell Bench Press with Neutral Grip', 'Pectoraux', 'Haltères', '1. Take a haltère in each hand and lay back onto a flat banc. vos pieds should be flat on le sol and your omoplates retracted.
2. Maintaining a neutral grip, paumes vers each other, begin with vos bras extended directly above you, perpendiculaire à le sol. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Begin le mouvement by flexing the coude, lowering the upper arms to the side. Descend until the haltères are to your torse.
4. Pause, then extend the coude and Revenez en position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Bench_Press_with_Neutral_Grip/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dumbbell Bicep Curl', 'Biceps', 'Haltères', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec a haltère in each hand at arm''s length. Keep your coudes close to your torse and rotate the palms of vos mains until they are facing forward. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Now, keeping the upper arms stationary, expirez and curl the poids while contracting your biceps. Continue to raise the poids until your biceps are entièrement contracté and the haltères are at épaule level. Hold the contracted position for a brief pause as you squeeze your biceps.
3. Then, inspirez and Lentement, begin to lower the haltères back to the position de départ.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Bicep_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dumbbell Clean', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Haltères', '1. Begin standing with a haltère in each hand with vos pieds épaule width apart.
2. Lower the poids to le sol by flexing at the hanches and genous, pushing your hanches back until the haltères reach le sol. C''est votre position de départ.
3. To initiate le mouvement, violently jump upward by extending the hanches, genous, and chevilles to acclerate the poids upward. Maintaining a neutral grip on the haltères, keep the arms straight until full extension is reached.
4. After full extension, rebend the hanches and genous to receive the poids in a squat position. Allow the arms to bend, guiding the haltères to your épaules.
5. Upon receiving the poids in the squat position, extend the hanches and genous to finish in a standing position with the poids on your épaules.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Avant-bras, Fessiers, Bas du dos, Quadriceps, Épaules, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Clean/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dumbbell Floor Press', 'Triceps', 'Haltères', '1. Lay on le sol holding haltères in vos mains. Your genous can be bent. Begin with the poids fully extended above you.
2. Lower the poids until your upper arm comes in contact with le sol. You can tuck your coudes to emphasize triceps size and strength, or to focus on your poitrine angle vos bras to the side.
3. Pause at the bottom, and then bring the poids together at the top by extending through the coudes.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Floor_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dumbbell Flyes', 'Pectoraux', 'Haltères', '1. Allongez-vous sur un banc plat with a haltère on each hand resting on top of your cuisses. The palms of your hand will be facing each other.
2. Then using your cuisses to help raise the haltères, lift the haltères one at a time so you can hold them in front of you at épaule width with the palms of vos mains facing each other. Raise the haltères up like you''re pressing them, but stop and hold just before you lock out. C''est votre position de départ.
3. With a slight bend on your coudes in order to prevent stress at the biceps tendon, lower vos bras out at both sides in a wide arc until you feel a stretch on your poitrine. Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : Keep in mind that throughout le mouvement, the arms should remain stationary; le mouvement should only occur at the épaule joint.
4. Return vos bras back to the position de départ as you squeeze your poitrine muscles and Expirez. Conseil : Make sure to use the same arc of motion used to lower the poids.
5. Maintenez la position 1 seconde at the contracted position and Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Flyes/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dumbbell Incline Row', 'Milieu du dos', 'Haltères', '1. Using a neutral grip, lean into an incline banc.
2. Take a haltère in each hand with a neutral grip, beginning with the arms straight. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Retract the omoplates and flex the coudes to row the haltères to your side.
4. Pause at the top of the motion, and then Revenez en position de départ.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Avant-bras, Dos, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Incline_Row/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Dumbbell Incline Shoulder Raise', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Asseyez-vous sur un banc while holding a haltère on each hand on top of your cuisses.
2. Lift vos jambes up to kick the poids to your épaules and lean back. Position the haltères above your épaules with vos bras extended. The arms should be perpendiculaire à le sol with your paumes vers l''avant and knuckles pointing towards the ceiling. C''est votre position de départ.
3. While keeping the arms straight and locked, lift the haltères by raising the épaules from the banc as you Expirez.
4. Bring back the haltères to the position de départ as you Inspirez.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Dumbbell_Incline_Shoulder_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
